(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural organization of transfer RNA \(tRNA\) and the two-step enzymatic mechanism of tRNA charging by Aminoacyl-tRNA Synthetases.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   tRNA Structure and Aminoacyl-tRNA Synthetase Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of Transfer RNA \(tRNA\):) Tj
T*
(   - Cloverleaf Secondary Structure: Consists of \(a\) Acceptor Stem terminating in a conserved) Tj
T*
(   single-stranded 5'-CCA-3' sequence with a free 3'-OH group where the amino acid attaches; \(b\)) Tj
T*
(   D-loop containing modified dihydrouridine bases; \(c\) Anticodon Loop containing the triplet) Tj
T*
(   anticodon flanked by hypermodified bases; \(d\) Variable Loop \(extra arm\) whose length classifies) Tj
T*
(   tRNAs; and \(e\) T-psi-C Loop containing pseudouridine and ribothymidine.) Tj
T*
(   - L-Shaped Tertiary Structure: Coaxial stacking of the acceptor stem onto the T-arm, and the) Tj
T*
(   D-arm onto the anticodon arm forms a rigid L-shaped conformation \(~70 Angstroms between the) Tj
T*
(   anticodon and 3'-CCA end\) ensuring precise positioning within ribosomal A and P sites.) Tj
T*
(   2. Two-Step Charging Mechanism \(Aminoacylation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Adenylation/Activation\): The amino acid reacts with ATP within the enzyme's catalytic) Tj
T*
(   pocket, releasing inorganic pyrophosphate \(PPi\):) Tj
T*
(   Amino Acid + ATP <-> Aminoacyl-AMP + PPi. Pyrophosphatase rapidly hydrolyzes PPi to 2 Pi,) Tj
T*
(   driving the reaction forward.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Transfer\): The aminoacyl group is transferred to the terminal adenosine of the tRNA:) Tj
T*
(   Aminoacyl-AMP + tRNA <-> Aminoacyl-tRNA + AMP.) Tj
T*
(   - Class Distinction: Class I synthetases aminoacylate the 2'-OH of the terminal ribose \(later) Tj
T*
(   shifted to 3'-OH via transesterification\), while Class II synthetases transfer the aminoacyl) Tj
T*
(   group directly to the 3'-OH.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe Crick's Wobble Hypothesis and explain how non-standard base pairing provides economy and flexibility in codon translation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Crick's Wobble Hypothesis:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - Watson-Crick base pairing is strictly enforced at codon positions 1 and 2 \(pairing with) Tj
T*
(   anticodon bases 36 and 35\).) Tj
T*
(   - Spatial steric freedom \('wobble'\) exists at the 3rd base of the codon \(pairing with the 1st) Tj
T*
(   base, position 34, of the anticodon at the 5' end of the anticodon loop\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Allowed Wobble Pairings \(Anticodon Base 34 vs Codon Base 3\):) Tj
T*
(   - C at 5' anticodon pairs ONLY with G at 3' codon \(Strict 1:1 fidelity\).) Tj
T*
(   - A at 5' anticodon pairs ONLY with U at 3' codon.) Tj
T*
(   - U at 5' anticodon can pair with A or G \(recognizes both purines\).) Tj
T*
(   - G at 5' anticodon can pair with C or U \(recognizes both pyrimidines\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inosine \(I, formed by deamination of adenine by ADAT\) can pair with three bases: U, C, or A.) Tj
T*
(   3. Biological Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - Economy of tRNA Genes: A minimum of only 31 tRNA species are required to translate all 61) Tj
T*
(   sense codons in eukaryotic/prokaryotic cytoplasm, rather than 61 distinct tRNAs.) Tj
T*
(   - Kinetic Advantage: Wobble pairing creates weaker hydrogen bonding at the 3rd position,) Tj
T*
(   accelerating the rate of tRNA dissociation from the ribosome during translation elongation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
