(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Architecture of 70S and 80S Ribosomes:) Tj
T*
(   1. Prokaryotic 70S Ribosome:) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Mass: ~2.5 MDa; dimensions ~200 x 220 Angstroms.) Tj
T*
(   - Small Subunit \(30S\): Composed of 16S rRNA \(1,542 nt\) and 21 ribosomal proteins \(S1-S21\).) Tj
T*
(   Responsible for decoding and monitoring mRNA-tRNA codon-anticodon fidelity.) Tj
T*
(   - Large Subunit \(50S\): Composed of 23S rRNA \(2,904 nt\), 5S rRNA \(120 nt\), and 31 ribosomal) Tj
T*
(   proteins \(L1-L36\). Contains the catalytic Peptidyl Transferase Center \(PTC\) and the polypeptide) Tj
T*
(   exit tunnel.) Tj
T*
(   2. Eukaryotic 80S Ribosome:) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Mass: ~4.0 - 4.5 MDa; expanded by eukaryotic-specific ribosomal expansion segments) Tj
T*
(   \(ES\).) Tj
T*
(   - Small Subunit \(40S\): Composed of 18S rRNA \(1,869 nt\) and 33 proteins \(eS1-eS33\). Matches mRNA) Tj
T*
(   codons with aminoacyl-tRNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Large Subunit \(60S\): Composed of 28S rRNA \(~4,700 nt\), 5.8S rRNA \(160 nt\), 5S rRNA \(120 nt\),) Tj
T*
(   and 47 proteins \(eL1-eL47\). Contains the peptidyl transferase ribozyme \(28S rRNA\) and) Tj
T*
(   regulatory surface binding sites for eEFs and signal recognition particles \(SRP\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
