(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the step-by-step mechanism of translation initiation in prokaryotes, highlighting the functions of IF1, IF2, and IF3.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Prokaryotic Translation Initiation Pathway:) Tj
T*
(   1. Ribosome Dissociation and Subunit Priming:) Tj
T*
(   - Free 70S ribosomes dissociate into 30S and 50S subunits.) Tj
T*
(   - IF3 binds to the 30S subunit at the E-site interface, physically preventing premature) Tj
T*
(   reassociation with the 50S subunit and ensuring mRNA binding fidelity.) Tj
T*
(   - IF1 binds to the 30S A-site, blocking initiator tRNA from binding there and guiding it) Tj
T*
(   strictly into the P-site.) Tj
T*
(   2. mRNA and Initiator tRNA Recruitment \(30S Initiation Complex\):) Tj
T*
(   - The 30S subunit binds mRNA by base-pairing between the anti-Shine-Dalgarno sequence of 16S) Tj
T*
(   rRNA \(3'-UCCUCCA-5'\) and the purine-rich Shine-Dalgarno consensus \(5'-AGGAGG-3'\) located 6-10) Tj
T*
(   nucleotides upstream of the AUG start codon.) Tj
T*
(   - IF2-GTP forms a ternary complex with formylmethionyl-tRNA \(fMet-tRNA_f^Met\) and escorts it) Tj
T*
(   directly into the partial P-site, establishing codon-anticodon pairing with AUG.) Tj
T*
(   3. 70S Initiation Complex Assembly:) Tj
T*
(   - Base-pairing of fMet-tRNA triggers a conformational switch in the 30S subunit, signaling IF3) Tj
T*
(   release.) Tj
T*
(   - The 50S large subunit docks onto the 30S complex.) Tj
T*
(   - Subunit docking stimulates the intrinsic GTPase activity of IF2; GTP hydrolysis causes) Tj
T*
(   conformational ejection of IF2-GDP and IF1.) Tj
T*
(   - The fully assembled 70S initiation complex contains fMet-tRNA in the P-site, with a vacant) Tj
T*
(   A-site ready to receive the second aminoacyl-tRNA.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 5:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the eukaryotic cap-dependent translation initiation pathway, including the 43S Pre-Initiation Complex, scanning, and 80S assembly.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Eukaryotic Cap-Dependent Translation Initiation:) Tj
T*
(   1. Assembly of the 43S Pre-Initiation Complex \(PIC\):) Tj
T*
(   - Free 40S subunit binds eIF1, eIF1A, eIF3, and eIF5.) Tj
T*
(   - eIF2 binds GTP and Met-tRNA_i^Met to form the Ternary Complex \(TC\).) Tj
T*
