/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   - The TC loads onto the 40S subunit, forming the 43S PIC.) Tj
T*
(   2. mRNA Activation by the eIF4F Complex:) Tj
T*
(   - The eukaryotic mRNA 5' 7-methylguanosine cap is bound by eIF4E.) Tj
T*
(   - eIF4G acts as a master scaffold protein, bridging eIF4E, poly\(A\)-binding protein \(PABP, bound) Tj
T*
(   to the 3' poly-A tail\), and eIF3, circularizing the mRNA into a 'closed-loop' topology.) Tj
T*
(   - eIF4A \(DEAD-box ATP-dependent RNA helicase\), assisted by eIF4B, unwinds secondary structures) Tj
T*
(   in the 5'-UTR.) Tj
T*
(   3. 48S Complex Formation, 5' -> 3' Scanning, and Start Codon Selection:) Tj
T*
(   - The 43S PIC is recruited to the 5' cap via the eIF3-eIF4G interaction.) Tj
T*
(   - The 43S complex scans linearly along the 5'-UTR in a 5' to 3' direction until it encounters) Tj
T*
(   the first AUG embedded within an optimal Kozak consensus sequence \(5'-ACCAUGG-3'\).) Tj
T*
(   4. 80S Assembly:) Tj
T*
(   - Codon recognition triggers eIF5-stimulated GTP hydrolysis by eIF2 and release of Pi.) Tj
T*
(   - eIF5B-GTP promotes joining of the 60S large subunit.) Tj
T*
(   - eIF5B hydrolyzes GTP, resulting in the ejection of eIF1, eIF2-GDP, eIF3, eIF5, and eIF5B,) Tj
T*
(   leaving an intact 80S ribosome with Met-tRNA_i^Met in the P-site.) Tj
T*
