/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 6:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the translation elongation cycle in bacteria, covering decoding by EF-Tu, peptide bond synthesis, and EF-G-mediated translocation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Translation Elongation Cycle in Bacteria:) Tj
T*
(   1. Aminoacyl-tRNA Delivery and Decoding \(A-site Binding\):) Tj
T*
(   - EF-Tu-GTP binds an aminoacyl-tRNA to form a ternary complex and delivers it to the ribosomal) Tj
T*
(   A-site.) Tj
T*
(   - Decoding: 16S rRNA bases A1492, A1493, and G530 flip out to inspect the minor groove of the) Tj
T*
(   codon-anticodon duplex.) Tj
T*
(   - Cognate matching triggers GTP hydrolysis by EF-Tu; EF-Tu-GDP dissociates, and the) Tj
T*
(   aminoacyl-tRNA accommodates fully into the peptidyl transferase center \(PTC\).) Tj
T*
(   - EF-Ts acts as a guanine nucleotide exchange factor \(GEF\), converting EF-Tu-GDP back to) Tj
T*
(   EF-Tu-GTP.) Tj
T*
(   2. Peptidyl Transfer \(Peptide Bond Formation\):) Tj
T*
(   - The alpha-amino group of the A-site amino acid executes a nucleophilic attack on the ester) Tj
T*
(   carbonyl carbon of the peptidyl-tRNA in the P-site.) Tj
T*
(   - The 23S rRNA acts as an entropic trap and proton shuttle \(involving A2451\), synthesizing a) Tj
T*
(   peptide bond without external ATP/GTP input.) Tj
T*
(   - The nascent peptide chain is transferred to the A-site tRNA, leaving a deacylated tRNA in the) Tj
T*
(   P-site.) Tj
T*
(   3. Ribosome Translocation:) Tj
T*
(   - The tRNAs adopt hybrid states: deacylated tRNA shifts to P/E state, and peptidyl-tRNA shifts) Tj
T*
(   to A/P state.) Tj
T*
