(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the molecular regulation of the E. coli lac operon under dual control: negative regulation by Lac repressor and positive regulation by CAP-cAMP.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Dual Molecular Regulation of the lac Operon:) Tj
T*
(   1. Operon Structure:) Tj
T*
(   - Polycistronic structural genes: lacZ \(beta-galactosidase\), lacY \(lactose permease\), and lacA) Tj
T*
(   \(thiogalactoside transacetylase\), driven by promoter Plac and operator placO.) Tj
T*
(   - lacI gene \(upstream, constitutively expressed\) produces homotetrameric Lac repressor.) Tj
T*
(   2. Negative Control \(Lactose Availability\):) Tj
T*
(   - In the absence of lactose: Lac repressor homotetramer binds tightly to the primary operator) Tj
T*
(   \(O1\) and auxiliary operators \(O2, O3\), looping the intervening DNA and sterically preventing) Tj
T*
(   RNA polymerase from initiating transcription.) Tj
T*
(   - In the presence of lactose: Beta-galactosidase isomerizes lactose to allolactose \(inducer\).) Tj
T*
(   Allolactose binds the Lac repressor, inducing a conformational change that reduces its) Tj
T*
(   DNA-binding affinity 1000-fold, releasing it from the operator.) Tj
T*
(   3. Positive Control & Catabolite Repression \(Glucose Availability\):) Tj
T*
(   - Glucose is the preferred carbon source. High glucose inhibits adenylate cyclase and) Tj
T*
(   stimulates cAMP phosphodiesterase, resulting in low intracellular cAMP levels.) Tj
T*
(   - When glucose is depleted: Adenylate cyclase is activated, elevating intracellular cAMP.) Tj
T*
(   - cAMP binds Catabolite Activator Protein \(CAP / CRP\). The cAMP-CAP dimer binds a specific DNA) Tj
T*
(   site upstream of the promoter, bending the DNA by ~90 degrees and making direct protein-protein) Tj
T*
(   contacts with the alpha-CTD of RNA polymerase, stabilizing its open promoter complex.) Tj
T*
(   4. Summary of Operon Output:) Tj
T*
(   - +Glucose, -Lactose: Operon OFF \(Repressor bound, CAP absent\).) Tj
T*
(   - +Glucose, +Lactose: Basal / Low expression \(Repressor released, CAP absent\).) Tj
T*
(   - -Glucose, -Lactose: Operon OFF \(Repressor bound, CAP bound\).) Tj
T*
(   - -Glucose, +Lactose: Fully Activated / HIGH expression \(Repressor released, CAP-cAMP bound\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
