(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structure and regulatory function of Riboswitches in prokaryotic gene expression.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Structure and Mechanism of Riboswitches:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structural Architecture of Riboswitches:) Tj
T*
(   - Located within the 5' untranslated regions \(5'-UTRs\) of bacterial mRNAs, riboswitches are) Tj
T*
(   cis-acting structured RNA elements that modulate gene expression upon binding specific small) Tj
T*
(   metabolites without requiring protein factors.) Tj
T*
(   - Composed of two modular domains:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Aptamer Domain: A highly conserved, evolutionarily ancient three-dimensional tertiary RNA) Tj
T*
(   fold that binds its cognate ligand \(e.g., TPP, FMN, SAM, cobalamin, guanine, lysine\) with high) Tj
T*
(   affinity and exquisite selectivity.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Expression Platform: A downstream, structurally flexible RNA segment that undergoes) Tj
T*
(   conformational remodeling in response to ligand binding at the aptamer.) Tj
T*
(   2. Mechanisms of Gene Regulation:) Tj
T*
(   - Transcriptional Termination: Ligand binding to the aptamer stabilizes an alternative fold in) Tj
T*
(   the expression platform that forms an intrinsic Rho-independent terminator hairpin, prematurely) Tj
T*
(   terminating transcription. In the absence of ligand, an antiterminator forms, permitting full) Tj
T*
(   transcription.) Tj
T*
(   - Translational Repression: Ligand binding induces the formation of an RNA stem-loop that) Tj
T*
(   sequesters the Shine-Dalgarno \(SD\) sequence and/or AUG start codon, sterically blocking 30S) Tj
T*
(   ribosomal subunit binding.) Tj
T*
(   - Self-Cleaving Ribozymes \(e.g., glmS riboswitch\): Binding of glucosamine-6-phosphate activates) Tj
T*
(   the riboswitch to act as a ribozyme, self-cleaving its own mRNA to trigger rapid degradation.) Tj
T*
