(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Histone Code Hypothesis and Epigenetic Enzymology:) Tj
T*
(   1. Histone Code Hypothesis:) Tj
T*
(   - Formulated by Strahl and Allis, the hypothesis posits that multiple post-translational) Tj
T*
(   covalent modifications \(PTMs\) on flexible N-terminal histone tails \(acetylation, methylation,) Tj
T*
(   phosphorylation, ubiquitination\) act combinatorially to create a specific molecular barcode.) Tj
T*
(   - This barcode is recognized by effector protein complexes \('readers'\) that alter higher-order) Tj
T*
(   chromatin structure and govern transcriptional access.) Tj
T*
(   2. Histone Acetylation Dynamics:) Tj
T*
(   - Histone Acetyltransferases \(HATs, e.g., p300/CBP, Gcn5\): Transfer acetyl groups from) Tj
T*
(   acetyl-CoA to the epsilon-amino group of lysine residues \(e.g., H3K9ac, H3K27ac\). Neutralizing) Tj
T*
(   the positive charge abolishes electrostatic interactions with negatively charged DNA,) Tj
T*
(   decondensing chromatin into open euchromatin. Acetyl-lysines are recognized by) Tj
T*
(   Bromodomain-containing readers.) Tj
T*
(   - Histone Deacetylases \(HDACs, Classes I-IV\): Catalyze the hydrolytic removal of acetyl groups,) Tj
T*
(   restoring lysine positive charge, promoting chromatin compaction into heterochromatin, and) Tj
T*
(   repressing transcription.) Tj
T*
(   3. Histone Methylation Dynamics:) Tj
T*
(   - Histone Methyltransferases \(HMTs\): Transfer 1, 2, or 3 methyl groups from) Tj
T*
(   S-adenosylmethionine \(SAM\) to lysine or arginine residues without altering overall charge.) Tj
T*
(   - Functional Dualism:) Tj
T*
(   * Activating Marks: H3K4 trimethylation \(H3K4me3\) at promoters and H3K36me3 in actively) Tj
T*
(   transcribed gene bodies.) Tj
T*
(   * Repressive Marks: H3K9me3 \(constitutive heterochromatin, bound by HP1 chromodomain\) and) Tj
T*
(   H3K27me3 \(facultative heterochromatin, catalyzed by PRC2/EZH2 and bound by PRC1 chromodomain\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
