(   [Problem Statement]: Explain DNA methylation in eukaryotes, detailing the functions of DNMT1, DNMT3A/B, CpG islands, and TET-mediated active demethylation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   DNA Methylation and Demethylation in Eukaryotes:) Tj
T*
(   1. Molecular Chemistry and Pattern:) Tj
T*
(   - In mammals, DNA methylation consists of the covalent addition of a methyl group to carbon-5) Tj
T*
(   of cytosine \(forming 5-methylcytosine, 5mC\), predominantly occurring in symmetrical 5'-CpG-3') Tj
T*
(   dinucleotide contexts.) Tj
T*
(   2. DNA Methyltransferases:) Tj
T*
(   - De Novo Methyltransferases \(DNMT3A and DNMT3B\): Establish new methylation marks on) Tj
T*
(   unmethylated DNA substrates during gametogenesis and early embryonic development.) Tj
T*
(   - Maintenance Methyltransferase \(DNMT1\): Possesses strong preference for hemimethylated DNA) Tj
T*
(   generated during semi-conservative replication. Recruited to the replication fork by UHRF1, it) Tj
T*
(   copies methylation patterns onto the newly synthesized daughter strand with >99% fidelity.) Tj
T*
(   3. CpG Islands and Transcriptional Repression:) Tj
T*
(   - CpG Islands are GC-rich regions \(~0.5 - 2 kb\) located at the promoters of ~60-70% of) Tj
T*
(   mammalian genes, normally kept unmethylated in somatic cells.) Tj
T*
(   - Aberrant hypermethylation of CpG islands recruits Methyl-CpG-Binding Domain proteins \(MBDs,) Tj
T*
(   e.g., MeCP2\). MBDs recruit HDAC-containing corepressor complexes, condensing chromatin and) Tj
T*
(   causing stable, heritable gene silencing \(common in tumor suppressor inactivation\).) Tj
T*
(   4. TET-Mediated Active Demethylation:) Tj
T*
(   - Ten-Eleven Translocation \(TET1/2/3\) dioxygenases iteratively oxidize 5mC into) Tj
T*
(   5-hydroxymethylcytosine \(5hmC\), 5-formylcytosine \(5fC\), and 5-carboxylcytosine \(5caC\).) Tj
T*
(   - Thymine DNA Glycosylase \(TDG\) excises 5fC and 5caC, which are subsequently repaired back to) Tj
T*
(   unmodified cytosine via the Base Excision Repair \(BER\) pathway.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
