12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the architecture of Eukaryotic Promoters, Enhancers, and Insulators, explaining the role of the Mediator complex and Chromatin Looping.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Eukaryotic Promoters, Enhancers, Insulators, and Chromatin Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Promoters:) Tj
T*
(   - Sequence elements within ~50 bp of the transcription start site \(TSS\), including the TATA) Tj
T*
(   box, Initiator \(Inr\), Downstream Promoter Element \(DPE\), and TFIIB recognition element \(BRE\).) Tj
T*
(   - Serve as the assembly platform for the Pre-Initiation Complex \(PIC\) consisting of TFIID \(TBP) Tj
T*
(   + TAFs\), TFIIA, TFIIB, TFIIE, TFIIF, TFIIH, and RNA Polymerase II.) Tj
T*
(   2. Enhancers and the Mediator Complex:) Tj
T*
(   - Enhancers are distal cis-regulatory DNA elements \(spanning 200 bp - 1 kb\) containing) Tj
T*
(   clustered binding sites for sequence-specific transcription factors. They function) Tj
T*
(   independently of distance and orientation.) Tj
T*
(   - The Mediator Complex: A multi-subunit \(26-30 proteins\) molecular bridge that physically) Tj
T*
(   interacts with enhancer-bound transcription factors and the C-terminal domain \(CTD\) of RNA Pol) Tj
T*
(   II at the promoter, facilitating transcription initiation and elongation.) Tj
T*
(   3. Chromatin Looping and Topological Associating Domains \(TADs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Enhancer-promoter communication across megabase distances occurs via 3D chromatin loops.) Tj
T*
(   - Loop formation is driven by the ATP-dependent loop extrusion activity of Cohesin rings until) Tj
T*
(   blocked by boundary elements bound by the zinc-finger protein CTCF.) Tj
T*
(   4. Insulators / Boundary Elements:) Tj
T*
(   - Prevent inappropriate cross-activation: \(a\) Enhancer-blocking insulators positioned between) Tj
T*
(   an enhancer and promoter prevent interaction; \(b\) Barrier insulators prevent heterochromatin) Tj
T*
(   spreading into euchromatic domains.) Tj
