(   [Problem Statement]: Compare the structural motifs utilized by transcription factors to recognize DNA: Zinc Finger, Helix-Turn-Helix, Leucine Zipper, and Basic Helix-Loop-Helix.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Transcription Factor Structural DNA-Binding Motifs:) Tj
T*
(   1. Helix-Turn-Helix \(HTH\) Motif:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Composed of two alpha-helices separated by a short beta-turn. The C-terminal) Tj
T*
(   'recognition helix' inserts into the DNA major groove, making sequence-specific hydrogen bonds) Tj
T*
(   with base edges.) Tj
T*
(   - Examples: Bacterial lac and trp repressors, CAP, and eukaryotic Homeodomain proteins \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Hox factors\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Zinc Finger \(ZnF\) Motif:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Structural domain stabilized by coordination of a zinc ion \(Zn2+\).) Tj
T*
(   - C2H2 Finger: Two cysteines in a beta-hairpin and two histidines in an alpha-helix coordinate) Tj
T*
(   Zn2+. Multiple fingers arranged in tandem wrap around the DNA major groove, each finger) Tj
T*
(   recognizing a 3-bp triplet. \(e.g., TFIIIA, Sp1\).) Tj
T*
(   - C4 / Nuclear Receptor Finger: Coordinates two zinc ions using four cysteines each \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   Glucocorticoid and Estrogen receptors\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Basic Leucine Zipper \(bZIP\) Motif:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Amphipathic alpha-helix containing a heptad repeat of leucine residues that) Tj
T*
(   form a hydrophobic coiled-coil dimerization domain \('zipper'\).) Tj
T*
(   - The N-terminal basic region \(rich in Arg and Lys\) projects into the major groove on opposite) Tj
T*
(   sides of the DNA double helix.) Tj
T*
(   - Examples: c-Jun, c-Fos \(AP-1 complex\), CREB.) Tj
T*
(   4. Basic Helix-Loop-Helix \(bHLH\) Motif:) Tj
T*
(   - Architecture: Two amphipathic alpha-helices separated by a flexible, non-helical loop of) Tj
T*
