(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the biogenesis, processing, and mechanism of action of MicroRNAs \(miRNAs\) in eukaryotic post-transcriptional gene regulation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   MicroRNA Biogenesis, Processing, and Silencing Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   1. Transcription and Nuclear Processing:) Tj
T*
(   - miRNAs are transcribed by RNA Polymerase II as long primary transcripts \(pri-miRNAs\)) Tj
T*
(   possessing 5'-caps and 3'-poly-A tails with stem-loop hairpin structures.) Tj
T*
(   - Microprocessor Complex \(Drosha RNase III + DGCR8/Pasha cofactor\): DGCR8 measures ~11 bp from) Tj
T*
(   the single-strand/double-strand RNA junction and guides Drosha to cleave the hairpin base,) Tj
T*
(   generating a ~65-70 nt precursor miRNA \(pre-miRNA\) with a 2-nt 3' overhang.) Tj
T*
(   2. Cytoplasmic Export and Dicer Cleavage:) Tj
T*
(   - Pre-miRNA is recognized by Exportin-5 in complex with Ran-GTP and exported through the) Tj
T*
(   nuclear pore into the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   - Dicer \(cytoplasmic RNase III\) in complex with TRBP measures ~22 nt from the 3' overhang and) Tj
T*
(   cleaves the terminal loop, producing a ~22-bp miRNA duplex with 2-nt 3' overhangs at both ends.) Tj
T*
(   3. RISC Loading and Strand Selection:) Tj
T*
(   - The duplex is loaded into an Argonaute protein \(AGO1-4 in humans\) to form the pre-RISC.) Tj
T*
(   - Strand selection: The strand whose 5' end is thermodynamically less stable is retained as the) Tj
T*
(   'guide strand' \(mature miRNA\), while the 'passenger strand' is unwound and degraded.) Tj
T*
(   4. Target Recognition and Silencing:) Tj
T*
(   - Target specificity is determined primarily by the 'Seed Sequence' \(nucleotides 2-8 from the) Tj
T*
(   5' end of the guide miRNA\), which pairs with complementary sites in the 3'-UTR of target mRNAs.) Tj
T*
(   - In animals \(imperfect pairing\): Recruits GW182/TNRC6 scaffold proteins, which recruit the) Tj
T*
(   CCR4-NOT and PAN2-PAN3 deadenylase complexes, leading to poly\(A\) shortening, decapping by DCP2,) Tj
T*
(   5'->3' degradation by XRN1, and translational repression.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
