12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Contrast Small Interfering RNAs \(siRNAs\) with MicroRNAs \(miRNAs\) in origin, structure, complementarity, and biological silencing mode.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Comparative Analysis of siRNAs versus miRNAs:) Tj
T*
(   1. Origin and Precursors:) Tj
T*
(   - miRNA: Originates endogenously from dedicated host non-coding RNA genes or introns;) Tj
T*
(   transcribed as single-stranded pri-miRNA hairpins by RNA Pol II.) Tj
T*
(   - siRNA: Originates from exogenous sources \(viral RNA, synthetic double-stranded RNA\) or) Tj
T*
(   aberrant long double-stranded RNAs \(transposons, convergent transcripts\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Processing Machinery:) Tj
T*
(   - miRNA: Requires two-step compartmental processing: Drosha-DGCR8 in the nucleus followed by) Tj
T*
(   Dicer in the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   - siRNA: Bypasses Drosha entirely; directly cleaved from long dsRNA substrates in the cytoplasm) Tj
T*
(   by Dicer into 21-23 bp duplexes.) Tj
T*
(   3. Degree of Complementarity:) Tj
T*
(   - miRNA: Exhibits partial, imperfect complementarity to target mRNA \(primarily restricted to) Tj
T*
(   the 7-nt 5' seed region\). A single miRNA can regulate hundreds of different mRNAs.) Tj
T*
(   - siRNA: Exhibits 100% perfect Watson-Crick base-pairing across its entire 21-nt length with a) Tj
T*
(   single specific mRNA target.) Tj
T*
(   4. Mechanism of Gene Silencing:) Tj
T*
