(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the functions of Long Non-Coding RNAs \(lncRNAs\), using the mechanism of X-chromosome inactivation by Xist as a primary paradigm.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Long Non-Coding RNAs \(lncRNAs\) and X-Chromosome Inactivation by Xist:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Functional Modes of lncRNAs:) Tj
T*
(   - Transcripts longer than 200 nucleotides that lack protein-coding capacity, typically) Tj
T*
(   transcribed by RNA Pol II, spliced, and polyadenylated.) Tj
T*
(   - Archetypal Mechanisms: \(a\) Signal/Sensor: Reflects cellular state; \(b\) Decoy: Titrates away) Tj
T*
(   microRNAs \(sponges\) or transcription factors; \(c\) Guide: Directs chromatin-modifying enzymes to) Tj
T*
(   genomic loci; \(d\) Scaffold: Assembles multi-protein complexes.) Tj
T*
(   2. Paradigm: X-Chromosome Inactivation by Xist:) Tj
T*
(   - Dosage compensation in female mammals \(XX\) requires transcriptional silencing of one) Tj
T*
(   X-chromosome to equalize gene dosage with males \(XY\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inactivation is orchestrated by the 17-kb lncRNA Xist \(X-inactive specific transcript\),) Tj
T*
(   transcribed exclusively from the future inactive X \(Xi\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Silencing Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Step 1 \(Spreading in Cis\): Xist RNA does not diffuse into the nucleoplasm; instead, it coats) Tj
T*
(   the chromosome of origin in cis, utilizing chromatin architecture and 3D proximity.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 2 \(Epigenetic Silencer Recruitment\): Xist contains repetitive elements \(Repeat A-F\).) Tj
T*
(   Repeat A directly recruits the SPEN repressor protein, which recruits HDAC3 to deacetylate) Tj
T*
(   histones across the chromosome.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 3 \(Polycomb Repression\): Xist recruits Polycomb Repressive Complex 1 \(PRC1, via hnRNP K\)) Tj
T*
(   and PRC2, depositing repressive marks H2AK119ub and H3K27me3.) Tj
T*
(   - Step 4 \(Chromatin Compaction\): MacroH2A histone variants and DNA methyltransferases) Tj
T*
(   \(DNMT1/3B\) are recruited, transforming the chromosome into transcriptionally silent,) Tj
T*
(   heterochromatic Barr body.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
