(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the mechanism of the Integrated Stress Response \(ISR\) and the molecular switch governing ATF4 translation via upstream open reading frames \(uORFs\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Integrated Stress Response \(ISR\) and ATF4 Translational Control:) Tj
T*
(   1. Core Sensor Kinases of ISR:) Tj
T*
(   Diverse cellular stress triggers converge on the phosphorylation of a single serine residue) Tj
T*
(   \(Ser51\) on the alpha-subunit of eukaryotic initiation factor 2 \(eIF2-alpha\):) Tj
T*
(   - PERK: Activated by endoplasmic reticulum \(ER\) stress \(unfolded protein response\).) Tj
T*
(   - PKR: Activated by double-stranded RNA during viral infection.) Tj
T*
(   - GCN2: Activated by uncharged tRNAs during amino acid deprivation.) Tj
T*
(   - HRI: Activated by heme deficiency and oxidative stress.) Tj
T*
(   2. Global Translational Attenuation:) Tj
T*
(   - Phosphorylated eIF2-alpha acts as a competitive inhibitor of eIF2B \(the guanine nucleotide) Tj
T*
(   exchange factor\).) Tj
T*
(   - Sequestration of eIF2B prevents GDP-to-GTP exchange on eIF2, depleting the ternary complex) Tj
T*
(   \(eIF2-GTP-Met-tRNA_i\) and shutting down global protein translation to conserve cellular energy) Tj
T*
(   and resources.) Tj
T*
