(   3. Paradoxical Activation of ATF4 Translation:) Tj
T*
(   - While global translation drops, activating transcription factor 4 \(ATF4\) translation is) Tj
T*
(   dramatically induced.) Tj
T*
(   - The ATF4 5'-UTR contains two upstream open reading frames: uORF1 \(positive regulatory) Tj
T*
(   element\) and uORF2 \(inhibitory element overlapping the ATF4 coding frame out-of-phase\).) Tj
T*
(   - Under Non-Stressed Conditions \(Abundant Ternary Complex\): Ribosomes translate uORF1, rapidly) Tj
T*
(   re-acquire a new ternary complex, initiate at uORF2, terminate past the ATF4 start codon, and) Tj
T*
(   dissociate. Zero ATF4 is translated.) Tj
T*
(   - Under Stressed Conditions \(Scarce Ternary Complex\): Ribosomes translate uORF1 and resume) Tj
T*
(   scanning, but because ternary complex is scarce, re-initiation is delayed. The scanning 40S) Tj
T*
(   subunit bypasses the inhibitory uORF2 start codon and finally acquires the ternary complex just) Tj
T*
(   in time to initiate at the real ATF4 coding sequence.) Tj
T*
(   - ATF4 activates adaptive genes for amino acid transport, redox balance, and autophagy.) Tj
