(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the Ubiquitin-Proteasome System \(UPS\), covering E1, E2, E3 enzyme cascade, polyubiquitin linkages, and 26S proteasome degradation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Ubiquitin-Proteasome System \(UPS\):) Tj
T*
(   1. The Three-Enzyme Ubiquitination Cascade:) Tj
T*
(   Ubiquitin \(a conserved 76-amino-acid peptide\) is covalently attached to lysine residues of) Tj
T*
(   target proteins through an ATP-dependent sequential cascade:) Tj
T*
(   - E1 \(Ubiquitin-Activating Enzyme\): Consumes ATP to form a high-energy ubiquitin-adenylate) Tj
T*
(   intermediate, then links ubiquitin's C-terminal Gly76 to a catalytic cysteine on E1 via a) Tj
T*
(   thioester bond.) Tj
T*
(   - E2 \(Ubiquitin-Conjugating Enzyme\): Receives activated ubiquitin from E1 through) Tj
T*
(   trans-thiolation, forming an E2-ubiquitin thioester conjugate.) Tj
T*
(   - E3 \(Ubiquitin Ligase\): Recognizes specific substrate degradation motifs \(degrons\) and) Tj
T*
(   catalyzes or mediates the transfer of ubiquitin from E2 to the epsilon-amino group of a lysine) Tj
T*
(   residue on the substrate via an isopeptide bond. \(E3 determines substrate specificity\).) Tj
T*
(   2. Polyubiquitin Chain Topologies and Functional Outcomes:) Tj
T*
(   - Ubiquitin contains 7 internal lysine residues \(K6, K11, K27, K29, K33, K48, K63\).) Tj
T*
(   - K48-Linked Chains \(at least 4 ubiquitins\): Canonical degradation signal targeting substrates) Tj
T*
(   to the 26S proteasome.) Tj
T*
(   - K63-Linked Chains: Regulate non-proteolytic signaling, including DNA double-strand break) Tj
T*
(   repair, NF-kB activation, and endocytic receptor trafficking.) Tj
T*
(   3. Architecture and Proteolysis by the 26S Proteasome:) Tj
T*
(   - 19S Regulatory Particle \(Cap\): Contains polyubiquitin-binding receptors \(Rpn10, Rpn13\),) Tj
T*
(   deubiquitinases \(DUBs\) to recycle ubiquitin, and a hexameric ring of AAA+ ATPases that unfold) Tj
T*
(   the substrate and thread it into the core.) Tj
T*
(   - 20S Core Particle: A cylindrical stack of four heptameric rings \(alpha7-beta7-beta7-alpha7\).) Tj
T*
(   The central beta-rings house 6 catalytic threonine protease sites:) Tj
T*
(   * beta1: Caspase-like activity \(cleaves after acidic residues\).) Tj
T*
(   * beta2: Trypsin-like activity \(cleaves after basic residues\).) Tj
T*
(   * beta5: Chymotrypsin-like activity \(cleaves after hydrophobic residues\).) Tj
T*
(   - Substrates are degraded into short peptides 3-15 amino acids in length.) Tj
T*
