(   1. Biological Purpose:) Tj
T*
(   - An essential eukaryotic mRNA surveillance pathway that detects and degrades transcripts) Tj
T*
(   harboring premature termination codons \(PTCs\), preventing the accumulation of truncated,) Tj
T*
(   potentially dominant-negative proteins.) Tj
T*
(   2. The Exon Junction Complex \(EJC\) Flag:) Tj
T*
(   - During pre-mRNA splicing in the nucleus, a multi-protein complex called the EJC \(composed of) Tj
T*
(   eIF4A3, MAGOH, Y14, and MLN51\) is deposited exactly 20-24 nucleotides upstream of every) Tj
T*
(   exon-exon junction.) Tj
T*
(   - EJCs remain bound to mRNA during nuclear export into the cytoplasm.) Tj
T*
(   3. The Pioneer Round of Translation and Rule of 50-55 Nucleotides:) Tj
T*
(   - During the initial 'pioneer round' of translation \(mRNA bound to CBP80/CBP20\), the moving 80S) Tj
T*
(   ribosome physically strips EJCs off the transcript.) Tj
T*
(   - Normal Stop Codon: Located in the terminal exon; therefore, no EJCs remain downstream when) Tj
T*
(   the ribosome terminates.) Tj
T*
(   - Premature Termination Codon \(PTC\): If a stop codon occurs more than 50-55 nucleotides) Tj
T*
(   upstream of the final exon junction, the ribosome terminates prematurely while one or more EJCs) Tj
T*
(   remain downstream.) Tj
T*
(   4. NMD Activation and mRNA Destruction:) Tj
T*
(   - Stalled ribosome at the PTC recruits release factors eRF1/eRF3, which recruit the master NMD) Tj
T*
(   helicase UPF1.) Tj
T*
(   - Downstream EJC-associated factors UPF2 and UPF3 bridge to UPF1, forming the SURF complex) Tj
T*
(   \(SMG1-UPF1-eRF1-eRF3\).) Tj
T*
(   - SMG1 kinase phosphorylates UPF1.) Tj
T*
(   - Phospho-UPF1 triggers translation repression and recruits SMG6 \(endonuclease that cleaves) Tj
T*
(   mRNA at the PTC\) and SMG5/SMG7, which recruit decapping \(DCP2\) and deadenylation complexes for) Tj
T*
(   rapid 5'->3' \(XRN1\) and 3'->5' \(Exosome\) degradation.) Tj
T*
