12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the bacterial tmRNA \(transfer-messenger RNA\) rescue system for ribosomes stalled on non-stop mRNAs.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   The Bacterial tmRNA \(SsrA\) Ribosome Rescue System:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Problem of Stalled Ribosomes:) Tj
T*
(   - In bacteria, when an mRNA is cleaved or lacks a termination stop codon, translating ribosomes) Tj
T*
(   reach the 3' end and stall indefinitely without a stop codon or release factor, depleting the) Tj
T*
(   cellular pool of active ribosomes.) Tj
T*
(   2. Dual Structure of tmRNA \(SsrA\):) Tj
T*
(   - A unique 360-400 nt chimeric RNA molecule functioning as both a transfer RNA and a messenger) Tj
T*
(   RNA:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) tRNA-Like Domain \(TLD\): Folds into a structure mimicking the acceptor stem and T-arm of) Tj
T*
(   tRNA^Ala, complete with a 5'-CCA-3' end charged with alanine by alanyl-tRNA synthetase. It) Tj
T*
(   lacks an anticodon loop.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) mRNA-Like Domain \(MLD\): Contains an internal open reading frame encoding an 11-amino-acid) Tj
T*
(   peptide degradation tag \(ANDENYALAA in E. coli\) terminating in a standard stop codon.) Tj
T*
(   3. Step-by-Step Rescue Mechanism \(Trans-Translation\):) Tj
T*
(   - Alanyl-tmRNA binds Small Protein B \(SmpB\) and EF-Tu-GTP to form an active ternary complex.) Tj
T*
(   - SmpB mimics the missing anticodon loop and enters the empty A-site of the stalled ribosome.) Tj
T*
(   - The ribosome transfers the nascent truncated peptide onto the alanine of tmRNA.) Tj
T*
(   - Translocation: The damaged mRNA is ejected, and the ribosome switches templates onto the mRNA) Tj
T*
(   domain of tmRNA.) Tj
T*
(   - The ribosome translates the 11-amino-acid peptide tag and terminates normally at the tmRNA) Tj
T*
(   stop codon using RF1/RF2.) Tj
T*
(   4. Biological Outcome:) Tj
T*
