(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss Internal Ribosome Entry Sites \(IRES\) and explain how viral and cellular mRNAs bypass 5'-cap-dependent translation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Internal Ribosome Entry Sites \(IRES\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept and Discovery:) Tj
T*
(   - Discovered in picornaviruses \(poliovirus and encephalomyocarditis virus\) by Sonenberg and) Tj
T*
(   Wimmer, an IRES is a complex secondary/tertiary RNA structure located in the 5'-UTR that allows) Tj
T*
(   direct internal recruitment of ribosomal subunits, bypassing the 5' m7G cap and eIF4E) Tj
T*
(   requirement.) Tj
T*
(   2. Structural Classification of Viral IRES:) Tj
T*
(   - Type I / II \(Picornavirus, EMCV\): Require eIF4G and eIF4A \(but not eIF4E\) to recruit the 43S) Tj
T*
(   pre-initiation complex.) Tj
T*
(   - Type III \(Hepatitis C Virus, HCV\): Directly binds the 40S ribosomal subunit and eIF3 with) Tj
T*
(   high nanomolar affinity without requiring any eIF4 factors.) Tj
T*
(   - Type IV \(Dicistroviruses, Cricket Paralysis Virus, CrPV\): The most streamlined IRES known. It) Tj
T*
(   folds into a pseudoknotted structure that mimics a tRNA-mRNA complex, directly occupying the P) Tj
T*
(   and A sites of the 80S ribosome and initiating translation at an alanine codon with zero) Tj
T*
(   initiation factors and zero initiator tRNA.) Tj
T*
(   3. Cellular IRES and Physiological Importance:) Tj
T*
(   - During viral infection, poliovirus 2A protease cleaves host eIF4G, shutting down host) Tj
T*
(   cap-dependent translation while viral IRES translation thrives.) Tj
T*
(   - Cellular mRNAs encoding critical survival, angiogenic, or apoptotic proteins \(e.g., VEGF,) Tj
T*
(   c-Myc, BiP, Bcl-2\) harbor cellular IRES elements, ensuring their preferential translation) Tj
T*
(   during severe cellular stress, mitosis, hypoxia, or apoptosis when cap-dependent translation is) Tj
T*
(   silenced.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
