(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the role of Phase Separation and Membraneless Organelles \(Stress Granules and P-bodies\) in mRNA compartmentalization and decay.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Phase Separation, Stress Granules, and P-Bodies:) Tj
T*
(   1. Liquid-Liquid Phase Separation \(LLPS\) in the Cytoplasm:) Tj
T*
(   - Membraneless organelles assemble through multivalent, low-affinity interactions among) Tj
T*
(   proteins with Intrinsically Disordered Regions \(IDRs\) or prion-like domains, and ribonucleic) Tj
T*
(   acids \(RNA\), demixing into distinct liquid condensates.) Tj
T*
(   2. Processing Bodies \(P-bodies\):) Tj
T*
(   - Constitutive cytoplasmic foci specialized in mRNA storage, decapping, and degradation.) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Components: Enriched in mRNA decay machinery, including deadenylation complexes) Tj
T*
(   \(CCR4-NOT\), decapping enzymes \(DCP1/DCP2\), decapping activators \(LSM1-7, EDC3, Pat1\), 5'->3') Tj
T*
(   exonuclease XRN1, and Argonaute proteins.) Tj
T*
(   - Exclude ribosomal subunits and translation initiation factors \(non-translating pool\).) Tj
T*
(   3. Stress Granules \(SGs\):) Tj
T*
(   - Transient condensates that rapidly assemble specifically upon cellular stress \(e.g., heat) Tj
T*
(   shock, oxidative stress, viral infection\) following eIF2-alpha phosphorylation.) Tj
T*
(   - Molecular Components: Contain stalled 48S pre-initiation complexes, core initiation factors) Tj
T*
(   \(eIF4E, eIF4G, eIF4A, eIF3\), poly\(A\)-binding protein \(PABP\), and RNA-binding proteins with) Tj
T*
(   prion-like domains \(G3BP1, G3BP2, TIA-1, TIAR\).) Tj
T*
(   - Function: Act as triage hubs, shielding non-essential mRNAs from translation and damage) Tj
T*
(   during stress, sorting transcripts for either storage, transfer to P-bodies for destruction, or) Tj
T*
(   rapid re-entry into the polysome pool upon stress resolution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
