(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the mechanism of Programmed Ribosomal Frameshifting \(-1 PRF\) and its importance in retroviral and coronavirus gene expression.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Programmed Ribosomal Frameshifting \(-1 PRF\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Principle of Translational Frameshifting:) Tj
T*
(   - A non-canonical translational mechanism where translating ribosomes are programmed by) Tj
T*
(   specific mRNA architectural elements to slip backward by exactly one nucleotide into the -1) Tj
T*
(   reading frame, yielding two distinct functional proteins from a single mRNA transcript in) Tj
T*
(   defined stoichiometry.) Tj
T*
(   2. Required mRNA Structural Elements:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Heptanucleotide Slippery Sequence: Consensus motif 5'-X_XXY_YYZ-3' \(where XXX can be any) Tj
T*
(   three identical bases, YYY is AAA or UUU, and Z is A, C, or U\).) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Downstream Secondary Structure: A rigid pseudoknot or stable stem-loop located exactly 5 to) Tj
T*
(   9 nucleotides downstream of the slippery sequence.) Tj
T*
