(   3. Biophysical Slipping Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - As the ribosome translocates along the slippery sequence, its entry into the mRNA tunnel is) Tj
T*
(   physically blocked by the unwinding resistance of the stable downstream pseudoknot.) Tj
T*
(   - This mechanical tension pauses the ribosome over the slippery site. During the pause, the) Tj
T*
(   tRNA anticodons in the A and P sites detach from their original codons \(XXY and YYZ\) and slip) Tj
T*
(   backward by 1 base to pair with the -1 frame codons \(XXX and YYY\), maintaining at least 2 out) Tj
T*
(   of 3 base pairs.) Tj
T*
(   - Once translocated in the -1 frame, the ribosome resumes translation across the unfolded) Tj
T*
(   pseudoknot.) Tj
T*
(   4. Viral Examples and Stoichiometric Balance:) Tj
T*
(   - Retroviruses \(e.g., HIV-1\): Uses -1 PRF to express the Gag-Pol polyprotein at a fixed ~5-10%) Tj
T*
(   ratio relative to the structural Gag protein \(~20:1 ratio required for viral capsid and enzyme) Tj
T*
(   assembly\).) Tj
T*
(   - Coronaviruses \(e.g., SARS-CoV-2\): Utilizes -1 PRF at the boundary of ORF1a and ORF1b to) Tj
T*
(   express the RNA-dependent RNA polymerase \(RdRp / nsp12\) and other viral replication machinery.) Tj
T*
