(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the co-translational insertion of Selenocysteine \(the 21st amino acid\) and Pyrrolysine \(the 22nd amino acid\) during genetic decoding.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Non-Canonical Amino Acid Incorporation \(Selenocysteine & Pyrrolysine\):) Tj
T*
(   1. Selenocysteine \(Sec, U\): The 21st Amino Acid:) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Structure: Analog of cysteine where the sulfur atom is replaced by selenium) Tj
T*
(   \(possesses a lower pKa ~5.2, making it a superior nucleophile for redox catalysis in) Tj
T*
(   glutathione peroxidase, thioredoxin reductase\).) Tj
T*
(   - Recoding Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Encoded by the UGA stop codon \(normally Opal nonsense codon\).) Tj
T*
(   * Requires a cis-acting mRNA stem-loop called the SECIS \(Selenocysteine Insertion Sequence\)) Tj
T*
(   element, located in the 3'-UTR of eukaryotic mRNAs or immediately downstream of UGA in) Tj
T*
(   bacteria.) Tj
T*
(   * Biosynthesis: tRNA^Sec is charged with serine by Seryl-tRNA Synthetase \(SerRS\), then) Tj
T*
(   converted to Selenocysteyl-tRNA^Sec by Selenocysteine Synthase.) Tj
T*
(   * Delivery: Dedicated elongation factor SelB \(bacteria\) or eEFSec/SBP2 \(eukaryotes\) binds SECIS) Tj
T*
(   and delivers Sec-tRNA^Sec into the ribosomal A-site when UGA is in the decoding center,) Tj
T*
(   overriding translation termination.) Tj
T*
(   2. Pyrrolysine \(Pyl, O\): The 22nd Amino Acid:) Tj
T*
(   - Chemical Structure: A lysine derivative modified with a methylpyrroline ring, found in) Tj
T*
(   methanogenic archaea and select bacteria for methylamine methyltransferase enzymes.) Tj
T*
(   - Recoding Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   * Encoded by the UAG stop codon \(Amber codon\).) Tj
T*
(   * Unlike selenocysteine, pyrrolysine possesses its own dedicated Pyrrolysyl-tRNA Synthetase) Tj
T*
(   \(PylRS\), which directly charges pyrrolysine onto tRNA^Pyl without needing a second amino acid) Tj
T*
(   intermediate.) Tj
T*
(   * Delivered to the UAG codon by standard elongation factor EF-Tu in the presence of a) Tj
T*
(   downstream pyrrolysine insertion sequence \(PYLIS\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
