(   - Standard transcription factors cannot access their recognition sequences when DNA is wrapped) Tj
T*
(   around histone octamers in condensed heterochromatin.) Tj
T*
(   - Pioneer Factors \(e.g., FoxA/HNF3, GATA, Oct4, Sox2\): Possess specialized winged-helix or HMG) Tj
T*
(   structural domains that recognize target sequence motifs exposed on the outer surface of) Tj
T*
(   nucleosomal DNA.) Tj
T*
(   - They bind tightly closed heterochromatin without displacing histones initially, serving as a) Tj
T*
(   beacon that recruits ATP-dependent chromatin remodelers and histone acetyltransferases.) Tj
T*
(   2. ATP-Dependent Chromatin Remodeling:) Tj
T*
(   - Large multi-protein machines that use energy from ATP hydrolysis to alter histone-DNA) Tj
T*
(   contacts, classified into four major families: SWI/SNF, ISWI, CHD, and INO80.) Tj
T*
(   3. Mechanism of the SWI/SNF \(BAF/PBAF\) Complex:) Tj
T*
(   - Core Catalytic Engine: Contains an essential SWI2/SNF2-family DNA translocase ATPase subunit) Tj
T*
(   \(SMARCA4/BRG1 or SMARCA2/BRM\) and bromodomains.) Tj
T*
(   - DNA Translocation and Loop Propagation:) Tj
T*
(   * The translocase anchors onto the nucleosomal core particle at superhelical location 2 \(SHL2\).) Tj
T*
(   * Consuming 1 ATP per base pair, it pumps DNA around the histone octamer, generating local) Tj
T*
(   torsional strain and peeling a wave of DNA off the histone surface \(DNA loop propagation\).) Tj
T*
(   * This pushes or 'slides' the histone octamer along the DNA fiber or completely evicts histone) Tj
T*
(   H2A-H2B dimers or the full octamer.) Tj
T*
(   - Result: Exposes previously occluded promoters and enhancers, allowing basal transcription) Tj
T*
(   factors \(TFIID\) and RNA Polymerase II to dock and initiate transcription.) Tj
T*
