(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss Epigenetic Inheritance through Mitotic and Meiotic Divisions, highlighting DNA methylation maintenance, histone inheritance, and genomic imprinting.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   Epigenetic Inheritance, Histone Segregation, and Genomic Imprinting:) Tj
T*
(   1. Mitotic Epigenetic Inheritance:) Tj
T*
(   - Faithful transmission of gene expression patterns across cell divisions without altering the) Tj
T*
(   primary DNA sequence:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) DNA Methylation Maintenance: During DNA replication, hemimethylated CpG sites are) Tj
T*
(   recognized by UHRF1, which recruits DNMT1 to methylate the newly synthesized nascent strand,) Tj
T*
(   restoring the symmetrical methylation pattern.) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Histone Mark Inheritance: During replication fork transit, parental histone \(H3-H4\)2) Tj
T*
(   tetramers are distributed randomly to the two daughter DNA duplexes, while new \(H3-H4\)2) Tj
T*
(   tetramers are deposited by histone chaperones \(CAF-1, Asf1\). Reader-writer complexes \(such as) Tj
T*
(   PRC2 via EED binding to existing H3K27me3\) recognize modifications on old histones and deposit) Tj
T*
(   the identical mark onto adjacent newly incorporated histones.) Tj
T*
(   2. Genomic Imprinting:) Tj
T*
(   - An epigenetic phenomenon in mammals where a gene is expressed in a parent-of-origin-specific) Tj
T*
(   manner \(monallelic expression\), while the other parental allele is epigenetically silenced.) Tj
T*
(   - Driven by differentially methylated regions \(DMRs\) established in the male or female germline) Tj
T*
(   by DNMT3A/3L that resist post-fertilization genome-wide demethylation waves.) Tj
T*
(   - Paradigm: Igf2 / H19 Locus on Chromosome 11:) Tj
T*
(   * Maternal Allele: The Imprinting Control Region \(ICR\) is unmethylated, allowing insulator) Tj
T*
(   protein CTCF to bind. CTCF blocks downstream enhancers from reaching the Igf2 promoter,) Tj
T*
(   diverting them to drive H19 expression. Igf2 is silenced.) Tj
T*
(   * Paternal Allele: The ICR is methylated during spermatogenesis. Methylation prevents CTCF) Tj
T*
(   binding and silences H19. Enhancers bypass the methylated ICR and activate Igf2. Igf2 is) Tj
T*
(   expressed.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
